  <h2>About the ANU School of Cybernetics</h2>

  <p>
    The <a href="https://cybernetics.anu.edu.au">School of Cybernetics</a> at the
    Australian National University takes a systems-oriented approach to understanding
    and shaping technology in society. The School&rsquo;s
    <a href="https://cybernetics.anu.edu.au/cybernetic-studio/"
      >Cybernetic Studio</a
    > develops hands-on resources and runs workshops exploring the social, technical,
    and political dimensions of emerging technologies.
  </p>

  <img
    src="/assets/images/workshop-3.avif"
    alt="LLMs Unplugged workshop in action"
  />

  <p>
    <em>LLMs Unplugged</em> reflects the School&rsquo;s commitment to making sophisticated
    technical concepts accessible to diverse audiences and fostering critical engagement
    with AI systems that increasingly mediate how we work, learn, and communicate.
    Understanding how these systems actually work&mdash;not through metaphor or handwaving
    but through direct experience&mdash;is what we&rsquo;re all about.
  </p>

